 "- **Boolean mask** — An array of True/False used to select elements (arr[arr > 0]). The idiomatic way to filter data without loops.",
 "- **View vs copy** — Slicing returns a view (shared memory); fancy indexing returns a copy. Mutating a view mutates the original — know which one you hold.",
 "- **Axis** — The dimension an operation reduces or acts along. axis=0 vs axis=1 confusion is a rite of passage; draw the array and point at the axis.",
 "- **Seed** — The starting state of a pseudorandom generator. Setting it makes 'random' splits, shuffles, and initializations reproducible across runs.",
